// Secrets.example.xcconfig
//
// Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (which is gitignored) and fill in the
// real value. NEVER commit `Secrets.xcconfig` — this repo is public.
//
// APP_KEY is the shared secret the backend requires as the `X-App-Key` header
// on every request. It MUST match the `APP_KEY` set in the backend's .env /
// Railway environment. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
//
// Wiring (already done for the RecipeApp target; only step 0 is per-clone):
//   0. Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` and set a real APP_KEY (below).
//   - Secrets.xcconfig is set as the RecipeApp target's base configuration
//     (Debug + Release), so it defines the APP_KEY build setting.
//   - The committed `ios/RecipeApp-Info.plist` (the target's INFOPLIST_FILE)
//     carries `APP_KEY = $(APP_KEY)`; Xcode expands it at build time and merges
//     it into the app's Info.plist, where RecipeKit's AppConfig reads it.
//   NOTE: a custom `INFOPLIST_KEY_APP_KEY` build setting does NOT work — Xcode
//   only injects its own known INFOPLIST_KEY_* keys into a generated plist, so
//   the value must go through a physical INFOPLIST_FILE as above.

APP_KEY = replace-with-a-real-secret
